# http_ping.hal — a minimal HTTP liveness checker.

Accept one command-line argument: a URL.

Issue a single HTTP GET against it with a 5-second timeout. Print one
of:

    OK <status-code> <url>
    FAIL <reason> <url>

Exit 0 on any 2xx response. Exit 1 on non-2xx. Exit 2 on a network
or timeout error.

No redirects needed. No auth. No retries.

If no argument is provided the app should return error. Do not imeplement with an example url. this is production code